  "id": "Compound::DB00734 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Risperidone, Paliperidone, and their derivatives are all agents affecting the nervous system and are linked to Cyp2d6 through a shared mechanism of binding. The evidence suggests that Risperidone and Paliperidone, both belonging to the class of organofluorine compounds, exert their effects by interacting with Cyp2d6, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in drug metabolism. The lowest common ancestor of Risperidone and Paliperidone is classified as an agent affecting the nervous system, indicating a common pharmacological profile. This shared pathway implies that the interaction between Risperidone and Cyp2d6 may be mediated through a common mechanism, possibly involving the organofluorine compound class. The consistent binding of Paliperidone to Cyp2d6 across different paths supports the notion of a direct pharmacological interaction, though the exact mechanism of how Risperidone influences Cyp2d6 remains to be fully elucidated.",
